        "original_id": "d8dfd61c-f472-59ec-bc1c-1b30005e06c4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Maurice Level, Alice Hoffman\n- Places: Paris, Pigalle district\n- Organizations: le Théâtre du Grand-Guignol\n- Roles: writer, novelist, young-adult writer, children's writer\n- Topics: macabre short stories, fiction, drama, Practical Magic, film adaptation\n\nFacts:\n- Maurice Level was born on August 29, 1875, and died on April 15, 1926.\n- Maurice Level was a French writer of fiction and drama who specialized in macabre short stories.\n- Maurice Level's macabre short stories were regularly printed in Paris newspapers and were sometimes staged by le Théâtre du Grand-Guignol in Paris's Pigalle district.\n- le Théâtre du Grand-Guignol was a repertory company devoted to melodramatic productions that emphasized blood and gore.\n- Alice Hoffman was born on March 16, 1952.\n- Alice Hoffman is an American novelist and a writer of young-adult and children's books.\n- Alice Hoffman is best known for her 1995 novel Practical Magic.\n- Practical Magic was adapted into a 1998 film of the same name.",
